{
    "_comment": "THE ROOT IS A NODE. There is no `menu` in this config at all: the shell contributes the SPACE (zones, layers, stages, toolbar, overlays, theme) and nothing else. Every navigable position, starting with the primary options in the left rail, is a C_YUI_NODE — the root's children, projected into zones. `menu.primary.render` always was a per-zone projection; now it has an owner that can hold it. One route entry ('/') owns the whole url space, so nothing below is declared anywhere.",
    "shell": {
        "_zones_comment": "Note what is NOT here: no zone declares `host: menu.<id>`. The rail and the bottom bar have no menu to host — the ROOT NODE projects its children into them (projection.zone + yui_shell_zone). The shell still owns the space: it builds the zones, applies their breakpoints and hosts the stage.",
        "zones": {
            "top": {
                "host": "toolbar",
                "show_on": "*"
            },
            "left": {
                "show_on": ">=desktop"
            },
            "bottom": {
                "show_on": "<desktop"
            },
            "center": {
                "host": "stage.main"
            }
        },
        "stages": {
            "main": {
                "zone": "center",
                "default_route": "/"
            }
        },
        "tree": {
            "base_route": "/",
            "stage": "main",
            "node_id": "root",
            "label": "Home",
            "tree_version": "1.0.0",
            "_projection_comment": "The root projects its children into ZONES of the space: a vertical rail on desktop, an icon bar at the bottom on mobile. index and chrome are the same here because the rail is standing chrome — it does not come and go with the position.",
